    "english":  "Yesterday, you and I chased the swarming bees from the flower-buds\nand played upon the white sandy beach washed by the receding tide,\nsurrounded by the backwaters and fragrant shoreline groves.\nBeyond that innocent play, we have done nothing in secret;\nand even if gossip were abroad, no stranger knows our quiet tryst.\nWhy then, my companion, did mother look upon us with such knowing eyes,\nand seeing the blue neytal flowers blooming like wide eyes\nalong the creek where herons hunt for silver shrimp,\nsay nothing today about sending us out to gather the fresh blossoms?",
